# Workflow-edit exemption — one exemption binds to one reviewed change.
#
# The change: wiring `check-fabro-graph-validity` into `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
# as a fail-closed job, so an invalid factory graph cannot reach master through a
# path that never runs the host pre-push. The gate itself already merged (PR 2435,
# c162939b); what is missing is venue coverage on the merge path.
#
# The named work item carries `approval:workflow-edit`, applied by the maintainer
# on 2026-09-10 as part of the re-dispatch rider on bd-ib-6t4. That item's
# description and comments hold the provenance, because a label alone cannot show
# who authorized it or for which change.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE EDIT IS PRESENT. A Fabro factory run CANNOT carry
# the `.github/workflows/` half of this change: `check-no-workflow-edits` verifies
# the approval label through `bd`, no `bd` exists inside the sandbox, and the guard
# fails closed at exit 2 with no environment escape by design. Measured in the
# bd-ib-6t4 sandbox on 2026-09-10, with this very declaration in place. The
# workflow edit therefore lands maintainer-side, alongside this declaration, per
# the factory-branch boundary's "restore that file, publish the rest, report the
# dropped diff" rule. Landing them together is what makes this declaration true.
work_item=bd-ib-6t4
reason=Wire check-fabro-graph-validity into ci.yml as a fail-closed required job (LIVESPEC_FABRO_GRAPH_VALIDATION=fail_when_fabro_absent) so an invalid factory graph cannot merge through a path that skips the host pre-push. Root-cause fix for two all_conditional_edges outages (2026-07-16 and release 0.146.0 on 2026-09-09), each of which took the whole factory down. Authorized by the maintainer's approval:workflow-edit label on bd-ib-6t4, 2026-09-10.
